{
  "body" : "You are designing a dreamy cinematic night portrait with glowing urban aesthetics.\n\nCONTENT BRIEF\n- Primary subject: {{subject}}\n- Scene or environment: {{setting}}\n- On-image text or tagline: {{copy}}\n\nSTYLE DIRECTION\n- Genre / medium: night-time editorial photography with cinematic aesthetics\n- Composition: 16:10 landscape (~1536×1024), foreground subject placed slightly off-center with dynamic movement; background dominated by bokeh city lights and urban structures\n- Lens / camera: medium focal length (~50mm), wide aperture (~f/1.8), shallow depth of field creating soft, circular bokeh; moderate motion blur capturing movement\n- Lighting: warm artificial street lighting, soft and diffused, with dynamic streaks and occasional lens flares\n- Color palette and grading: warm golden tones contrasted with cooler hues from urban night lighting; slightly desaturated colors with a dreamy glow\n- Texture / surface: soft focus and smooth texture with subtle film-like grain\n- Post-processing: halation, bloom effects around light sources, lens flare, and motion blur to enhance the dreamlike quality\n- Mood: ethereal, introspective, cinematic, nostalgic\n- References: Wong Kar-wai’s visual style, Cinestill 800T halation, dreamy street photography\n\nDESIGN RULES\n- Aspect: 16:10 landscape (~1536×1024) suitable for hero banner placement or editorial use\n- Maintain subject focus with soft edges and shallow depth of field\n- Ensure glowing and blurred light sources dominate the background to enhance the cinematic mood\n\nAVOID\n- No harsh daylight or high-key lighting\n- No sharp shadows or high contrast\n- No crisp focus across the entire frame\n- No cluttered or overly detailed backgrounds\n- No bright colors without complementary muted tones\n- No flat or overly sterile lighting\n\nAdditional constraints: {{extra}}\n\n——————\nSubject: {{subject}}\nSetting: {{setting}}\nCopy: {{copy}}\nExtra notes: {{extra}}",
